%description:

Tcp.minRexmitTimeout:free -- the RTO is the estimate when it is above the minimum.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the lower limit of the retransmission timeout".

The classes: binds (a minimum above SRTT + 4 RTTVAR; 1s is the default) and free (a minimum
below it; 200ms is the value of LinuxTcp), on a path whose round trip is 100 ms. The code:
TcpAlgorithmBase::rttMeasurementComplete(). This test separates "free" from "binds".

Host under test: host1, which sends 10000 bytes on a path with a round trip of 100 ms.
Observation: level 2, the signal rto after the first measurement is the estimate,
SRTT + 4 RTTVAR = 0.3 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.minRexmitTimeout
%# class: free
%# value: 0.2s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMinRexmitTimeoutFree")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("rto")
                  .first()
                  .assertValueBetween(0.29, 0.32)
                  .describe("the RTO after the first measurement, the estimate")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMinRexmitTimeoutFree compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout = 0.2s    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 25ms
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMinRexmitTimeoutFree: PASS
